1
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,737
PREVIOUSLY

2
00:00:07,487 --> 00:00:08,947
Hey, it's me, Uncle.

3
00:00:09,031 --> 00:00:10,365
[Jinwoo] Miss Jeong Jian?

4
00:00:10,782 --> 00:00:13,493
Uh, Mr. Jeong Jinman has been found dead.

5
00:00:15,662 --> 00:00:17,205
[Jian] This is what my uncle sold?

6
00:00:17,289 --> 00:00:18,332
You being serious?

7
00:00:18,415 --> 00:00:19,416
THEN… IS JEONG JINMAN DEAD?

8
00:00:20,584 --> 00:00:21,793
THEN… YOU'LL DIE TODAY TOO,
JEONG JIAN?

9
00:00:21,877 --> 00:00:23,086
[thudding sound]
[inhales sharply]

10
00:00:24,254 --> 00:00:25,255
[gasps]

11
00:00:26,757 --> 00:00:28,383
[screams, grunts]

12
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,053
[Seongjo] Wow!

13
00:00:31,136 --> 00:00:33,013
The veteran warriors
have all gathered together!

14
00:00:35,265 --> 00:00:36,391
[shatters]

15
00:00:36,475 --> 00:00:38,685
The first person who manages
to kill Jinman's niece

16
00:00:38,769 --> 00:00:39,895
or captures her alive

17
00:00:39,978 --> 00:00:41,355
will bring home a big fat bonus.

18
00:00:41,438 --> 00:00:43,023
All right, the rabbit hunt begins!

19
00:00:43,482 --> 00:00:45,067
[thuds, whirs]

20
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:47,027
[whirring]

21
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,155
[Jinman] Listen up, Jeong Jian.

22
00:00:50,238 --> 00:00:51,490
Whatever scares you,

23
00:00:51,573 --> 00:00:53,950
keep your eyes open and face it head-on.

24
00:00:54,659 --> 00:00:57,371
[Minhye] I see that you don't think
before you act.

25
00:00:57,454 --> 00:00:59,122
That's not what your uncle would do.

26
00:00:59,206 --> 00:01:01,416
Yes, on the floor
where your uncle did most of his work

27
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,627
is a door that opens into Murthehelp.

28
00:01:05,045 --> 00:01:06,797
-No way.
-[thuds]

29
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:08,006
[Jeongmin] It actually exists.

30
00:01:08,799 --> 00:01:10,342
[high-pitched ringing]

31
00:01:10,425 --> 00:01:12,052
Wait, no, please, it's too bright.

32
00:01:12,135 --> 00:01:14,096
You haven't answered my question yet!

33
00:01:14,179 --> 00:01:15,222
[Brother] Jeong Jian!

34
00:01:15,305 --> 00:01:16,473
D-d-don't trust him!

35
00:01:16,556 --> 00:01:17,557
[gasps]

36
00:01:17,641 --> 00:01:18,850
Jeongmin!

37
00:01:19,643 --> 00:01:21,019
[♪ tense music playing]

38
00:01:21,103 --> 00:01:23,313
[Seongjo] But there is something
you should know.

39
00:01:23,939 --> 00:01:26,817
Your Uncle Jinman killed
a lot of people too.

40
00:01:27,609 --> 00:01:29,736
[Bale] You and I both get paid
to kill people.

41
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:31,780
Stop pretending to be righteous.

42
00:01:31,863 --> 00:01:32,948
It makes me sick.

43
00:01:33,031 --> 00:01:35,409
In the end, you and I
are more alike than you think.

44
00:01:36,827 --> 00:01:41,581
[both grunting]

45
00:01:46,503 --> 00:01:47,963
[Bale] If you don't kill me here,

46
00:01:48,046 --> 00:01:49,423
I'll kill everyone.

47
00:01:49,506 --> 00:01:53,343
All your friends, and family, and anyone
who has anything to do with you.

48
00:01:54,719 --> 00:01:56,388
-[gasps]
-[Kuma] You must be Jeong Jian.

49
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:59,599
-You really do take after your uncle.
-[heavy breathing]

50
00:02:05,564 --> 00:02:06,648
[Jian] That you, Master?

51
00:02:07,149 --> 00:02:08,608
[Pasin] We don't have time, Jian.

52
00:02:08,692 --> 00:02:09,860
Bale's after you.

53
00:02:09,943 --> 00:02:11,445
[Bale] You're up, you two.

54
00:02:11,528 --> 00:02:12,988
Go and handle this.

55
00:02:13,071 --> 00:02:14,364
[engine revving]

56
00:02:14,448 --> 00:02:15,615
[crashes]

57
00:02:15,699 --> 00:02:17,242
[♪ tense music playing]

58
00:02:18,326 --> 00:02:19,953
Hey there, twins.

59
00:02:20,036 --> 00:02:21,747
Today is the day we go to Hell.

60
00:02:23,665 --> 00:02:25,500
[fighting grunts]

61
00:02:34,426 --> 00:02:35,469
[grunts]

62
00:02:35,552 --> 00:02:37,471
Jian, you better run!

63
00:02:37,554 --> 00:02:39,055
-Minhye!
-Get outta here!

64
00:02:39,139 --> 00:02:40,307
[cries]

65
00:02:42,601 --> 00:02:44,770
[Jinman] I'll give you two options
to choose from.

66
00:02:44,853 --> 00:02:47,939
But ultimately,
the choice is yours to make.

67
00:02:49,191 --> 00:02:51,234
-[Jian screams]
-[gunshots]

68
00:02:52,152 --> 00:02:54,738
[Seongjo exclaiming]

69
00:02:55,530 --> 00:02:56,531
[gunshot]

70
00:02:56,615 --> 00:02:59,576
[♪ tense music playing]

71
00:03:09,044 --> 00:03:10,045
[inhales]

72
00:03:10,128 --> 00:03:13,215
[screaming]

73
00:03:14,508 --> 00:03:15,842
[Bale] It should be me…

74
00:03:15,926 --> 00:03:17,677
[♪ soft tense music playing]

75
00:03:18,261 --> 00:03:19,721
who takes his life away.

76
00:03:22,265 --> 00:03:23,266
Don't you think?

77
00:03:27,312 --> 00:03:30,857
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

78
00:03:30,941 --> 00:03:34,110
[footsteps thudding]

79
00:03:34,194 --> 00:03:36,821
[breathing heavily]

80
00:03:46,706 --> 00:03:49,626
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

81
00:03:57,175 --> 00:03:58,176
[staff 1] Team Leader?

82
00:04:03,223 --> 00:04:05,308
[alarm wailing]

83
00:04:05,392 --> 00:04:06,643
What's going on?

84
00:04:11,565 --> 00:04:12,774
[grunts, groans]

85
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:14,276
-[grunts]
-[groans]

86
00:04:17,529 --> 00:04:19,906
[staff 2] It's the server room! Move, now!

87
00:04:20,907 --> 00:04:23,493
[alarm wailing continues]
STYLE
::cue()

88
00:04:30,041 --> 00:04:31,293
[clicks]

89
00:04:31,376 --> 00:04:33,295
[sighs]

90
00:04:39,968 --> 00:04:44,514
[warped droning intensifies]

91
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:48,518
[explosion]

92
00:04:53,315 --> 00:04:55,442
[♪ muffled suspenseful music playing]

93
00:04:55,525 --> 00:04:57,777
[high-pitched ringing]

94
00:05:15,629 --> 00:05:18,840
[♪ tense music intensifies]

95
00:05:21,885 --> 00:05:26,181
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

96
00:05:32,896 --> 00:05:35,815
EPISODE 01
JINMAN ON THE SAME DAY

97
00:05:38,985 --> 00:05:42,405
[♪ pensive music playing]

98
00:06:09,015 --> 00:06:11,893
[Jeongmin] Wait! Jeong Jinman!

99
00:06:12,519 --> 00:06:15,021
You have to let me down!

100
00:06:15,105 --> 00:06:16,314
Hey, you fucker!

101
00:06:19,192 --> 00:06:20,360
[door opens]

102
00:06:36,543 --> 00:06:38,253
[Jeongmin laughing]

103
00:06:38,336 --> 00:06:42,549
[laughing continues]

104
00:06:42,632 --> 00:06:46,136
-[machines thudding]
-[alarm beeping]

105
00:06:51,891 --> 00:06:53,727
[cell phone buzzing]

106
00:06:58,273 --> 00:07:00,233
[Jinwoo] Time of death is 1900 hours.

107
00:07:00,316 --> 00:07:02,444
I've transferred the body
to the Hansarang Gyeongae Hospital

108
00:07:02,527 --> 00:07:04,154
mortuary in Yecheong County.

109
00:07:05,321 --> 00:07:07,824
His niece Jeong Jian
is his only surviving family.

110
00:07:07,907 --> 00:07:09,951
No need to involve Yecheong Police.

111
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:17,041
[keys jingling]

112
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:28,011
[lock clanking]

113
00:07:43,485 --> 00:07:45,153
[beeping]

114
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:48,198
[lock clicks open]

115
00:08:00,835 --> 00:08:03,797
[♪ soft music playing]

116
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:06,257
[clicking]

117
00:08:07,550 --> 00:08:09,219
[Jinwoo] North Korean defector.

118
00:08:10,094 --> 00:08:12,514
Can't believe you're still alive.

119
00:08:12,597 --> 00:08:14,808
Well, that's because security
in South Korea's

120
00:08:14,891 --> 00:08:16,351
-become soft since I've been gone.
-[chuckles]

121
00:08:17,268 --> 00:08:18,269
Look at you.

122
00:08:18,353 --> 00:08:20,146
You don't look like
you've come across any guards.

123
00:08:20,230 --> 00:08:21,231
-Hey.
-[chuckles]

124
00:08:21,314 --> 00:08:22,649
[laughs]

125
00:08:24,734 --> 00:08:26,152
Officer Jinwoo.

126
00:08:26,236 --> 00:08:27,320
Pasin.

127
00:08:27,987 --> 00:08:29,864
-[speaking Thai] Jinwoo-krap.
-[in English] How are you?

128
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:32,075
You're working out too much.

129
00:08:32,158 --> 00:08:34,702
Yeah, well, for a cop,
you're a skinny little bitch.

130
00:08:34,786 --> 00:08:35,787
[chuckles]

131
00:08:35,870 --> 00:08:37,247
[door slides open]

132
00:08:50,468 --> 00:08:53,388
Starting now, we have 62 hours.

133
00:08:55,223 --> 00:08:56,266
Babylon…

134
00:08:57,267 --> 00:08:58,393
took our bait.
STYLE
::cue()

135
00:08:59,227 --> 00:09:01,563
[associate] From the outside,
this place looks exactly like

136
00:09:01,646 --> 00:09:03,523
every other run-of-the-mill rice factory.

137
00:09:04,649 --> 00:09:07,443
One of the buildings even operates
as a rice warehouse.

138
00:09:07,986 --> 00:09:09,237
But it's just a cover.

139
00:09:10,029 --> 00:09:14,159
A full one-kilometer radius spanning
all directions is completely flat land.

140
00:09:15,243 --> 00:09:17,620
Anyone approaching
will be spotted immediately.

141
00:09:18,329 --> 00:09:19,956
This place is a fortress.

142
00:09:21,457 --> 00:09:23,585
[whooshing]

143
00:09:27,255 --> 00:09:28,298
[whirs]

144
00:09:28,381 --> 00:09:30,842
[alarm wailing]

145
00:09:32,719 --> 00:09:34,721
The assholes have upgraded.

146
00:09:34,804 --> 00:09:36,723
Now we have to get around all of that.

147
00:09:38,766 --> 00:09:39,767
[sighs]

148
00:09:39,851 --> 00:09:43,396
[associate] Most of Babylon's facilities
are installed on their basement floors.

149
00:09:43,479 --> 00:09:45,023
The armory is on basement four.

150
00:09:45,106 --> 00:09:47,358
The situation room, basement two.

151
00:09:47,442 --> 00:09:49,819
There's a 30-millimeter AA gun
on the rooftop.

152
00:09:50,612 --> 00:09:53,072
[associate] Ninety-six soldiers
of Babylon's mobile force

153
00:09:53,156 --> 00:09:54,574
are active until 6:00 p.m.

154
00:09:54,657 --> 00:09:58,328
But, Jinman, it's supposed
to be a surprise, isn't it?

155
00:09:59,704 --> 00:10:01,581
It would be better
to kill Bale somewhere else.

156
00:10:05,293 --> 00:10:06,336
[Jinman] This is the target.

157
00:10:07,086 --> 00:10:08,171
[burbling]

158
00:10:08,254 --> 00:10:09,547
[Pasin] The server?

159
00:10:09,631 --> 00:10:12,258
[Jinman] It houses all
of Babylon's classified files.

160
00:10:12,342 --> 00:10:14,928
They've been around
since the military dictatorship.

161
00:10:15,011 --> 00:10:17,347
Babylon's carried out
all the intelligence operations,

162
00:10:17,430 --> 00:10:19,224
kidnappings, and assassinations

163
00:10:19,307 --> 00:10:20,934
on behalf of every changing regime.

164
00:10:21,017 --> 00:10:23,895
Including selling North Korea weapons
behind our government's back.

165
00:10:24,854 --> 00:10:27,273
In the conflict zones
of Southeast and Central Asia,

166
00:10:27,357 --> 00:10:30,318
they made arms deals
with both rebels and government forces.

167
00:10:30,401 --> 00:10:33,029
Political coups were engineered
for their own gain.

168
00:10:33,112 --> 00:10:34,197
Decades of client lists,

169
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,615
intelligence operatives,

170
00:10:35,698 --> 00:10:37,242
all their contract kill data.

171
00:10:37,325 --> 00:10:39,035
Everything top secret
is being kept in there.

172
00:10:43,456 --> 00:10:45,875
Bale killed hundreds of civilians
during operations.

173
00:10:47,043 --> 00:10:49,045
That evidence is buried there as well.

174
00:10:50,046 --> 00:10:51,923
This is our bargaining chip.

175
00:10:52,882 --> 00:10:55,718
Babylon will have no choice
but to be kept in check.

176
00:10:55,802 --> 00:10:58,638
The result is a maintained
state of neutrality.

177
00:11:00,932 --> 00:11:02,308
If our plan fails…

178
00:11:04,686 --> 00:11:07,814
this exhausting,
useless war will never end for us.

179
00:11:09,482 --> 00:11:12,527
Jian deserves to live a full
and peaceful life.

180
00:11:14,195 --> 00:11:15,405
[Jinman] We can't fail.

181
00:11:16,364 --> 00:11:18,491
Jian needs us to protect her
with this shield.

182
00:11:19,117 --> 00:11:20,785
[Jinwoo] Can't we just hack the data?

183
00:11:20,868 --> 00:11:22,453
Impossible. [clicks tongue]

184
00:11:22,537 --> 00:11:24,872
In order to keep it secure
and to prevent overheating,

185
00:11:24,956 --> 00:11:27,125
they keep it separate
from the general server room

186
00:11:27,208 --> 00:11:29,502
and store it independently underwater.

187
00:11:29,585 --> 00:11:31,004
This wall is made of concrete

188
00:11:31,087 --> 00:11:32,714
and serves as the firewall.

189
00:11:32,797 --> 00:11:34,007
[sighs]

190
00:11:34,090 --> 00:11:37,176
Even so, it has to be connected
to somewhere outside, right?

191
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:39,929
True, but it's still submerged underwater.

192
00:11:40,013 --> 00:11:41,014
[sighs]

193
00:11:41,097 --> 00:11:43,474
Ah, even a Kim Il Sung University elite

194
00:11:43,558 --> 00:11:44,684
is stumped, huh? [clicks tongue]

195
00:11:44,767 --> 00:11:46,769
Collect the reward and report the spy.

196
00:11:48,021 --> 00:11:49,897
This asshole's useless.

197
00:11:49,981 --> 00:11:51,524
What do you propose instead?

198
00:11:52,608 --> 00:11:54,068
We're removing the whole thing.

199
00:11:54,694 --> 00:11:56,446
[associate] At 1500 hours every day,

200
00:11:56,529 --> 00:11:59,115
the server is raised
from the water tank for inspection.

201
00:11:59,198 --> 00:12:01,284
[Pasin] Great. We'll hack it then.

202
00:12:01,826 --> 00:12:05,038
What the hell, how'd this Thai idiot
ever work with Babylon?

203
00:12:05,705 --> 00:12:07,999
You should keep your dumb mouth shut.
[clicks tongue]

204
00:12:08,082 --> 00:12:09,208
Watch your step, man.

205
00:12:09,292 --> 00:12:10,460
[water trickling]

206
00:12:10,543 --> 00:12:13,212
[machine whirring, beeping]

207
00:12:17,884 --> 00:12:19,093
[heavy thud]

208
00:12:25,516 --> 00:12:28,269
[♪ tense music playing]

209
00:12:31,356 --> 00:12:32,982
[associate] This is our chance.

210
00:12:33,066 --> 00:12:35,109
But we'll only have 20 minutes.

211
00:12:35,902 --> 00:12:39,405
Infiltrating the enemy network
and downloading the data that quickly?

212
00:12:39,989 --> 00:12:41,616
It's impossible even for Zuckerberg.

213
00:12:41,699 --> 00:12:42,825
Zuck, who… who is that?

214
00:12:42,909 --> 00:12:44,202
Just say hacking, come on.

215
00:12:44,285 --> 00:12:45,453
Thai genius.

216
00:12:45,536 --> 00:12:46,746
You're gonna have to be the one

217
00:12:46,829 --> 00:12:48,998
that brings the new-model bomb
to my location.

218
00:12:49,082 --> 00:12:50,333
Oh, yeah?

219
00:12:50,416 --> 00:12:51,417
Why is that?

220
00:12:51,501 --> 00:12:52,585
Because you're good.

221
00:12:52,668 --> 00:12:54,629
[Jinman] We can't take weapons
inside Babylon,

222
00:12:54,712 --> 00:12:56,339
so we'll go through the armory.

223
00:12:56,422 --> 00:12:58,925
Team leaders and up
can carry personal sidearms,

224
00:12:59,008 --> 00:13:00,927
but they're only allowed
to access the ammo

225
00:13:01,010 --> 00:13:02,470
during an active operation.

226
00:13:03,721 --> 00:13:04,722
[smacks lips]

227
00:13:05,348 --> 00:13:06,974
The armory has what we need.

228
00:13:07,058 --> 00:13:08,893
We'll have to raid it for weapons.

229
00:13:08,976 --> 00:13:11,646
[Jinman] In the explosive section,
you'll find the E5 bombs,

230
00:13:11,729 --> 00:13:14,899
which were specially manufactured
as miniature bunker-busters.

231
00:13:14,982 --> 00:13:18,403
With those, we'll blast into the rooms
above and below the server.

232
00:13:18,486 --> 00:13:21,406
I take the bombs
and blast it into the server?

233
00:13:21,489 --> 00:13:25,618
Pasin, you also have to plant a bomb
above the server on the first floor.
STYLE
::cue()

234
00:13:26,285 --> 00:13:27,495
That'll be really tough.

235
00:13:27,578 --> 00:13:29,330
Why can't you stop complaining?

236
00:13:30,373 --> 00:13:31,541
I have it just as bad.

237
00:13:31,624 --> 00:13:32,959
Look over there.

238
00:13:33,042 --> 00:13:34,836
It's not always about the big things.

239
00:13:34,919 --> 00:13:37,964
The most physical things
aren't always the toughest.

240
00:13:40,174 --> 00:13:41,425
My issue…

241
00:13:42,426 --> 00:13:45,012
is figuring out what bait
will reel this guy in.

242
00:13:46,764 --> 00:13:47,807
[sighs]

243
00:13:53,354 --> 00:13:54,897
BEAUTIFUL FEMALE MASSEUSE!!
ALWAYS ON STANDBY!!

244
00:13:54,981 --> 00:13:56,440
PREMIUM-QUALITY MASSAGE
GRAND OPENING SPECIAL!

245
00:13:59,569 --> 00:14:00,820
[sighs]

246
00:14:02,530 --> 00:14:03,573
DELETE MESSAGES

247
00:14:10,079 --> 00:14:12,582
[door opens, closes]

248
00:14:12,665 --> 00:14:14,584
DELETE ALL

249
00:14:14,667 --> 00:14:15,668
[scoffs]

250
00:14:15,751 --> 00:14:18,212
To defeat your enemies,
you must think like your enemies.

251
00:14:18,296 --> 00:14:21,174
[crickets chirping]

252
00:14:23,384 --> 00:14:24,844
[keyboard clacking]

253
00:14:27,305 --> 00:14:28,347
[beeping]

254
00:14:33,477 --> 00:14:35,313
THE PROFESSOR HAS SELECTED
TOMORROW'S SURGE STOCK.

255
00:14:38,733 --> 00:14:40,401
South Koreans and capitalism.

256
00:14:40,484 --> 00:14:42,195
Gets them every time.

257
00:14:42,278 --> 00:14:45,865
[beeping]

258
00:14:48,242 --> 00:14:49,619
KIM JUNGHO
SECURITY TEAM LEADER

259
00:14:49,702 --> 00:14:51,162
[whirring]

260
00:14:54,457 --> 00:14:56,250
That's cool.

261
00:14:56,334 --> 00:14:58,461
KIM JUNGHO
SECURITY TEAM LEADER

