[exasperated sigh]

530
00:33:46,671 --> 00:33:49,674
That was tougher than clearing mines
on the demarcation line.

531
00:33:50,175 --> 00:33:51,217
[sighs]

532
00:33:51,301 --> 00:33:52,302
[inhales]

533
00:33:53,053 --> 00:33:54,721
I'm moving to my next position.
STYLE
::cue()

534
00:33:54,804 --> 00:33:55,889
[elevator bell dings]

535
00:33:56,890 --> 00:33:59,601
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

536
00:34:12,197 --> 00:34:13,823
[metallic clanking]

537
00:34:13,907 --> 00:34:17,660
[metallic clanking continues]

538
00:34:22,332 --> 00:34:23,875
[trilling]

539
00:34:26,252 --> 00:34:27,253
[beeps]

540
00:34:27,337 --> 00:34:29,506
[♪ upbeat music playing]

541
00:34:34,427 --> 00:34:35,678
Okay.

542
00:34:35,762 --> 00:34:37,806
Cheolseung's moved
into his second position.

543
00:34:37,889 --> 00:34:39,099
Standby.

544
00:34:39,182 --> 00:34:41,976
[♪ upbeat music continues]

545
00:34:53,279 --> 00:34:54,697
[Jinwoo] Ten minutes remaining.

546
00:34:55,448 --> 00:34:57,075
Armory CCTVs?

547
00:34:57,158 --> 00:34:58,576
[Cheolseung] They're no problem.

548
00:34:59,369 --> 00:35:00,620
DANGER

549
00:35:11,965 --> 00:35:13,550
I'm returning my gun.

550
00:35:16,177 --> 00:35:17,178
[beeps]

551
00:35:18,346 --> 00:35:19,973
[whirring]

552
00:35:25,770 --> 00:35:28,898
EXPLOSIVE MATERIALS
WARNING EXPLOSIVE MATERIAL

553
00:35:28,982 --> 00:35:31,609
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

554
00:35:50,587 --> 00:35:51,588
[beeps]

555
00:36:21,534 --> 00:36:22,744
[alarm wails]

556
00:36:22,827 --> 00:36:23,995
[clicks]

557
00:36:24,412 --> 00:36:27,123
[whirring, rattling]

558
00:36:28,875 --> 00:36:30,335
[whirring]

559
00:36:30,418 --> 00:36:32,504
[trills, beeps]

560
00:36:33,463 --> 00:36:35,465
[Jinwoo] It's almost time.
What's going on?

561
00:36:39,010 --> 00:36:40,970
[whirring]

562
00:36:41,054 --> 00:36:44,474
[machine beeping]

563
00:36:49,771 --> 00:36:51,064
What is it?

564
00:36:51,147 --> 00:36:52,732
Someone tell me what's going on.

565
00:36:52,816 --> 00:36:54,025
[heavy thud]

566
00:36:59,113 --> 00:37:00,532
[scraping]

567
00:37:03,660 --> 00:37:07,330
[♪ tense music playing]

568
00:37:34,566 --> 00:37:35,650
[grunts]

569
00:37:41,656 --> 00:37:43,658
Now is your only chance.

570
00:37:58,590 --> 00:37:59,841
[electric crackling]

571
00:38:07,515 --> 00:38:08,808
[whirs]

572
00:38:12,270 --> 00:38:13,313
[grunts]

573
00:38:13,396 --> 00:38:15,899
[panting]

574
00:38:19,027 --> 00:38:20,236
[door closes]
STYLE
::cue()

575
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:21,321
Uh, Chief?

576
00:38:21,905 --> 00:38:24,782
I think we need to check
Team Leader Bale's location.

577
00:38:24,866 --> 00:38:26,117
Why?

578
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:28,786
I walked past him in the situation room
a few minutes ago,

579
00:38:28,870 --> 00:38:31,664
but then, two minutes later,
I ran into him on a different floor.

580
00:38:31,748 --> 00:38:34,751
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

581
00:38:50,016 --> 00:38:51,017
[grunts]

582
00:38:57,649 --> 00:38:58,775
[groans]

583
00:39:16,501 --> 00:39:19,629
[panting]

584
00:39:22,715 --> 00:39:24,008
Huh?

585
00:39:24,092 --> 00:39:26,302
Team Leader Bale has two cars on site?

586
00:39:30,848 --> 00:39:33,559
[♪ tense music playing]

587
00:39:38,147 --> 00:39:39,357
[creaking]

588
00:39:39,440 --> 00:39:42,485
[♪ tense music continues]

589
00:39:46,406 --> 00:39:47,740
[Jinman grunts]

590
00:39:49,033 --> 00:39:50,159
[strained grunt]

591
00:39:51,369 --> 00:39:52,370
[sighs]

592
00:40:04,257 --> 00:40:05,508
The inspection is complete.

593
00:40:06,884 --> 00:40:07,885
[beeps]

594
00:40:09,178 --> 00:40:10,263
[whirs]

595
00:40:18,771 --> 00:40:20,231
I have to go down.

596
00:40:20,314 --> 00:40:21,733
Something weird's going on.

597
00:40:21,816 --> 00:40:23,359
Hey, wait a sec.

598
00:40:23,443 --> 00:40:24,569
What are you going to do?

599
00:40:30,867 --> 00:40:33,327
[door whirs open]

600
00:40:34,412 --> 00:40:38,750
[machine beeping]

601
00:40:48,551 --> 00:40:50,970
[both grunting]

602
00:40:51,054 --> 00:40:52,138
[groans]

603
00:40:53,848 --> 00:40:54,849
[grunts]

604
00:40:54,932 --> 00:40:57,226
[breathing heavily]

605
00:40:57,894 --> 00:40:58,978
[loud thud]

606
00:40:59,062 --> 00:41:00,271
[Cheolseung panting]

607
00:41:03,900 --> 00:41:05,443
Ah, shit.

608
00:41:06,611 --> 00:41:08,946
[panting]

609
00:41:09,530 --> 00:41:10,615
[sighs]

610
00:41:11,407 --> 00:41:13,868
[panting]

611
00:41:15,328 --> 00:41:17,205
I took care of the first floor.

612
00:41:17,288 --> 00:41:20,041
I was waiting forever,
I thought you died in there.

613
00:41:21,793 --> 00:41:22,835
[exhales]

614
00:41:23,544 --> 00:41:25,296
Glad you're alive.

615
00:41:26,172 --> 00:41:27,381
I won't die today.

616
00:41:27,465 --> 00:41:29,884
[panting]

617
00:41:29,967 --> 00:41:30,968
Or ever.

618
00:41:33,930 --> 00:41:37,183
Check the route and radius of movement
to see where that vehicle came from,

619
00:41:37,266 --> 00:41:38,684
and run a malware scan.

620
00:41:38,768 --> 00:41:40,686
-We could've been hacked.
-Yes, sir.

621
00:41:42,980 --> 00:41:45,733
[drones whirring]

622
00:41:45,817 --> 00:41:48,236
[♪ intense music playing]

623
00:41:57,036 --> 00:41:58,204
[whirs]

624
00:41:58,955 --> 00:42:00,164
[beeping]

625
00:42:06,712 --> 00:42:07,922
[whirs]

626
00:42:08,005 --> 00:42:11,843
[beeping]

627
00:42:18,891 --> 00:42:22,603
[groaning]

628
00:42:22,687 --> 00:42:24,272
[Cheolseung]
Server room installation complete.

629
00:42:24,355 --> 00:42:25,523
Okay.

630
00:42:32,655 --> 00:42:34,448
Ah, shit.

631
00:42:35,408 --> 00:42:37,076
My location's been compromised.
STYLE
::cue()

632
00:42:46,502 --> 00:42:47,795
[staff] Team two has arrived.

633
00:42:47,879 --> 00:42:49,046
Ten minutes to entry.

634
00:42:49,547 --> 00:42:50,548
General.

635
00:42:52,008 --> 00:42:53,092
Jeong Jinman…

636
00:42:53,968 --> 00:42:55,386
Do you think he's still alive?

637
00:42:57,930 --> 00:42:58,973
[door opens]

638
00:43:04,312 --> 00:43:07,273
Sir, one of the drones has been shot,
and we've been hacked.

639
00:43:10,943 --> 00:43:12,904
What? What's wrong?

640
00:43:12,987 --> 00:43:17,325
[alarm wailing]

641
00:43:20,203 --> 00:43:22,788
Oh, shit. That son of a bitch.

642
00:43:26,834 --> 00:43:28,419
What's going on? Go find out.

643
00:43:32,965 --> 00:43:34,884
[explosion]

644
00:43:34,967 --> 00:43:36,802
[loud blast]

645
00:43:42,934 --> 00:43:46,187
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

646
00:43:55,321 --> 00:43:57,990
[♪ tense music playing]

647
00:44:41,284 --> 00:44:43,744
-[high-pitched warbling]
-[all groaning in pain]

648
00:44:43,828 --> 00:44:46,163
[groaning continues]

649
00:44:57,425 --> 00:45:00,052
17 MEO 4396

650
00:45:08,853 --> 00:45:11,480
[♪ tense music continues]

651
00:45:12,565 --> 00:45:13,941
[beeping]

652
00:45:14,025 --> 00:45:15,276
[explodes]

653
00:45:17,903 --> 00:45:20,865
[hissing]

654
00:45:45,348 --> 00:45:46,432
[Bale grunts]

655
00:45:47,767 --> 00:45:49,477
[Jinman grunts]

656
00:45:50,186 --> 00:45:51,187
[groans]

657
00:45:52,396 --> 00:45:54,523
-[grunts]
-[Jinman groans]

658
00:45:54,607 --> 00:45:57,401
[panting]

659
00:46:00,988 --> 00:46:02,281
[Bale] When I heard you were dead,

660
00:46:03,491 --> 00:46:05,242
I was so disappointed.

661
00:46:17,296 --> 00:46:19,423
[♪ dark, ominous music playing]

662
00:46:21,133 --> 00:46:22,134
What?

663
00:46:23,219 --> 00:46:24,303
You're not scared?

664
00:46:30,893 --> 00:46:33,979
[both grunting]
STYLE
::cue()

665
00:46:51,330 --> 00:46:52,998
[fierce grunts]

666
00:46:59,255 --> 00:47:01,048
[yells]

667
00:47:09,723 --> 00:47:11,058
[both groan]

668
00:47:11,142 --> 00:47:14,311
[♪ action music playing]

669
00:47:15,312 --> 00:47:16,772
[fighting grunts]

670
00:47:30,619 --> 00:47:32,538
-[Bale groans]
-[thuds]

671
00:47:32,621 --> 00:47:35,040
[panting]

672
00:47:35,124 --> 00:47:36,125
See you later.

673
00:47:40,921 --> 00:47:46,343
[inaudible screaming]

674
00:47:54,643 --> 00:47:58,230
[bomb timers beeping]

675
00:48:01,609 --> 00:48:04,111
[beeping continues]

676
00:48:04,195 --> 00:48:05,446
[explosion]

677
00:48:07,615 --> 00:48:09,617
[muffled explosion]

678
00:48:12,620 --> 00:48:15,206
[loud rumbling]

679
00:48:28,135 --> 00:48:29,136
[pants]

680
00:48:38,270 --> 00:48:40,439
[panting]

681
00:48:44,443 --> 00:48:45,569
[Yonghan] Jinman!

682
00:48:47,112 --> 00:48:48,447
It's over.

683
00:48:49,990 --> 00:48:51,534
It's time to end this.

684
00:48:51,617 --> 00:48:55,913
[drones whirring]

685
00:49:12,346 --> 00:49:14,014
[gunfire]

686
00:49:17,518 --> 00:49:20,187
[helicopter blades whirring]

687
00:49:31,699 --> 00:49:33,617
Shoot him down, idiots!

688
00:49:34,660 --> 00:49:36,203
[gunfire]

689
00:49:58,434 --> 00:50:01,270
[♪ tense music playing]

690
00:50:05,274 --> 00:50:06,275
[clatters]

691
00:50:24,585 --> 00:50:25,586
[sighs]

692
00:50:26,295 --> 00:50:30,674
[panting]
STYLE
::cue()

693
00:50:36,305 --> 00:50:39,308
[♪ somber music playing]

694
00:50:53,280 --> 00:50:54,448
[driver] It's dangerous out here.

695
00:50:54,531 --> 00:50:56,950
You should go back inside
and wait in the shopping mall.

696
00:50:57,034 --> 00:50:59,745
Sir. Someone is heading
this way right now.

697
00:51:01,914 --> 00:51:03,248
You just stay here.

698
00:51:04,083 --> 00:51:05,084
It's all right.

699
00:51:10,297 --> 00:51:12,591
[bird squawking]

700
00:51:16,345 --> 00:51:17,680
[driver] Are they one of ours?

701
00:51:18,931 --> 00:51:21,183
No, sir, they haven't been confirmed.

702
00:51:33,112 --> 00:51:35,489
[Jinwoo] Jinman, we're almost there.

703
00:51:36,156 --> 00:51:38,951
[labored breathing]

704
00:52:00,347 --> 00:52:02,349
[birds chirping]

705
00:52:06,603 --> 00:52:08,063
I know that man.

706
00:52:18,282 --> 00:52:19,283
[sighs]

707
00:52:22,077 --> 00:52:23,078
[grunts]

708
00:52:26,373 --> 00:52:29,460
[labored breathing]

709
00:52:33,338 --> 00:52:34,339
[relieved sigh]

710
00:52:36,175 --> 00:52:38,177
[♪ gentle music playing]

711
00:52:49,646 --> 00:52:51,315
[grunts, pants]

712
00:52:51,398 --> 00:52:53,650
[furious grunting]

713
00:53:10,876 --> 00:53:15,631
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

714
00:53:15,714 --> 00:53:17,674
[♪ dark, ominous music playing]

715
00:53:19,051 --> 00:53:22,095
[♪ upbeat music playing]

716
00:53:22,179 --> 00:53:24,598
[♪ electronic dance music playing]

717
00:53:29,645 --> 00:53:31,480
[indistinct chatter]

718
00:53:38,821 --> 00:53:41,740
SIGMA

719
00:53:42,324 --> 00:53:45,118
[cell phone vibrating]

720
00:53:45,244 --> 00:53:46,954
[vibrating continues]

721
00:53:47,913 --> 00:53:49,414
-Yeah?
-[Jun] Onee-chan,

722
00:53:49,498 --> 00:53:51,875
you're too old to be playing
around in clubs.

723
00:53:51,959 --> 00:53:53,377
I'm not playing.

724
00:53:53,460 --> 00:53:54,920
-I'm working.
-[Jun scoffs]

725
00:53:55,003 --> 00:53:56,296
[Jun] How'd you get in?

726
00:53:56,380 --> 00:53:59,716
Security must be slacking,
they let anyone in these days.

727
00:53:59,800 --> 00:54:01,385
You've got to be joking.

728
00:54:01,468 --> 00:54:04,263
I can get in wherever I want.

729
00:54:04,346 --> 00:54:06,181
[Jun laughing] Yeah, you wish.

730
00:54:08,058 --> 00:54:10,060
I'm working, stop interfering.

731
00:54:10,143 --> 00:54:11,353
What is it that you want?

732
00:54:11,436 --> 00:54:13,146
[Jun] The director is summoning you.

733
00:54:14,147 --> 00:54:16,358
What, why?

734
00:54:17,359 --> 00:54:19,194
-[sighs]
-[Jun] Jeong Jinman.

735
00:54:19,278 --> 00:54:20,362
Do you remember him?

736
00:54:24,241 --> 00:54:25,367
I remember.

737
00:54:27,452 --> 00:54:30,414
[♪ closing theme music playing]

